# COM-1: pin LF on everything a container reads directly. A CRLF shebang,
# nginx directive or entrypoint fails inside the image with confusing errors.
#
# This service is the first non-Go one, so the file list is not the same as
# services/gateway_dev/.gitattributes: there is no *.sql here, and *.json and
# env.json matter because nginx serves them and a BOM or CRLF would reach the
# browser. Unlike the root .gitattributes these are set without `text=`, which
# is the shape services/gateway_dev already uses.
#
# Do NOT run `git add --renormalize .` repo-wide after this (design/08-auth-skeleton-plan.md:19);
# only the paths this commit creates.
*.sh         eol=lf
Dockerfile   eol=lf
dockerfile   eol=lf
Jenkinsfile  eol=lf
nginx.conf   eol=lf
*.conf       eol=lf
*.yml        eol=lf
*.yaml       eol=lf
*.json       eol=lf
*.css        eol=lf
*.html       eol=lf
# Source files, for the same reason and one more: an editor on Windows can write
# CRLF into one of these without anyone noticing, which shows up as a whole-file
# diff in review even though the blob normalises. Declaring it here stops that at
# the source rather than at `prettier --check` in CI.
*.ts         eol=lf
*.js         eol=lf
*.vue        eol=lf
*.md         eol=lf
